File watching is platform-specific. The following examples wait for one real file-system event
instead of polling modification times.

### macOS and FreeBSD: `kqueue`

This example uses `kqueue` and `EVFILT_VNODE` to watch `build.zig`. Run it on macOS or FreeBSD,
then modify or rename the file from another terminal.

[]($code.siteAsset('src/file-system/kqueue.zig').language('zig'))

### Linux: `inotify`

This example uses `inotify` to watch the current directory. Run it on Linux, then create, modify,
move, or delete a file from another terminal.

[]($code.siteAsset('src/file-system/inotify.zig').language('zig'))
